{"author":{"id":"fa8586a84d377d0163bc90133d6fa21a62438d9387a725c881f9af5b108f10e0"},"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"fa8586a84d377d0163bc90133d6fa21a62438d9387a725c881f9af5b108f10e0"},"timestamp":1778325337,"metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDODbKJfs8AAAABBv-5Ew","github-url":"https://github.com/vmiklos/plees-tracker/issues/576#issuecomment-4412389651"},"nonce":"eREj87XO4Xn7A4BCwyafgolHstc=","message":"\u003e \u003e Not quite sure if this a bug or intentional.\n\u003e \n\u003e It's intentional: did you find the \"Ignore empty days when showing average of daily sums\" setting that is on by default, but you probably want to disable it? See https://vmiklos.hu/plees-tracker/usage.html#dashboard\n\nOh, perfect, that's exactly the setting I was looking for! Thanks a lot! (And oops, now I'm down to 7:26 daily average. But very useful/helpful to know.)\n\n\u003e For this, there is just a workaround: you can do a start, followed by a stop and then you can edit both if you go to the sleep activity. Various other stats want to know the start/stop time for each sleep, so a special sleep with no exact start/stop, just a duration would be a bit odd.\n\nYou mean adding a 0min. sleep event? And edit that to the real sleep time later? Not quite sure how that would help in my situation. Typically I notice a few days later that I must have forgotten to track a sleep interval. And then don't remember the exact time anymore.\n\n\u003e so a special sleep with no exact start/stop, just a duration would be a bit odd.\n\nI was thinking about something like a \"vacation mode\" interval. It would have an exact start+stop+duration. But this interval shouldn't modify the average stats and shouldn't add to total sleep durations.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"fa8586a84d377d0163bc90133d6fa21a62438d9387a725c881f9af5b108f10e0"},"timestamp":1778325390,"metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lALODbKJfs8AAAABBv-5E865dp7W"},"nonce":"mBTKZH23cTIEY0DnFO2V6ZWbDCA=","target":"cdff83d6070875f03d3b6693e33fb320f3388c30c7da43fe48ca9cfd2bf8e35f","message":"\u003e \u003e Not quite sure if this a bug or intentional.\n\u003e \n\u003e It's intentional: did you find the \"Ignore empty days when showing average of daily sums\" setting that is on by default, but you probably want to disable it? See https://vmiklos.hu/plees-tracker/usage.html#dashboard\n\nOh, perfect, that's exactly the setting I was looking for! Thanks a lot! (And oops, now I'm down to 7:26 daily average. But very useful/helpful to know.)\n\n\u003e For this, there is just a workaround: you can do a start, followed by a stop and then you can edit both if you go to the sleep activity. Various other stats want to know the start/stop time for each sleep, so a special sleep with no exact start/stop, just a duration would be a bit odd.\n\nYou mean adding a 0min. sleep event? And edit that to the real sleep time later? Not quite sure how that would help in my situation. Typically I notice a few days later that I must have forgotten to track a sleep interval. And then don't remember neither the exact time nor duration anymore.\n\n\u003e so a special sleep with no exact start/stop, just a duration would be a bit odd.\n\nI was thinking about something like a \"vacation mode\" interval. It would have an exact start+stop+duration. But this interval shouldn't modify the average stats and shouldn't add to total sleep durations.","files":null}]}